meta {
  name: Edit Request
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/requests/{{requestId}}/edit
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "purpose": "Updated purpose text",
    "description": "Updated description with more detail.",
    "assignedDept": "Software",
    "assignedDepts": null,
    "dueDate": "2026-06-30T18:00:00.000Z",
    "assignedPersonEmpId": "GN-2001",
    "assignedPersonName": "John Doe"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    console.log("✅ Request edited | ID:", res.body.id, "| Purpose:", res.body.purpose);
  } else if (res.status === 403) {
    console.log("❌ Forbidden — only the requestor can edit this request");
  } else if (res.status === 409) {
    console.log("🔒 Locked —", res.body.error);
  } else if (res.status === 404) {
    console.log("❌ Request not found");
  } else {
    console.log("❌", res.body.error);
  }
}

docs {
  # Edit Request

  Edits core fields of a request.
  - **Requestor (owner)** — allowed only while nobody else has approved, forwarded, marked Checking,
    closed, or replied in chat on the ticket.
  - **SuperUser** — allowed anytime.

  Each edit logs a system chat message ("Request edited by …").

  ## Editable fields (all optional — only send what you want to change)
  | Field                | Type     | Description                                      |
  |----------------------|----------|--------------------------------------------------|
  | purpose              | string   | Short summary of the request                     |
  | description          | string   | Full description                                 |
  | assignedDept         | string   | Primary assigned department                      |
  | assignedDepts        | string   | Comma-separated list of departments (or null)    |
  | dueDate              | ISO date | Due date (or null to clear)                      |
  | assignedPersonEmpId  | string   | Assigned person's employee ID (or null to clear) |
  | assignedPersonName   | string   | Assigned person's display name (or null to clear)|
  | ccDepts              | string   | Comma-separated CC departments (or "" to clear)  |
  | ccEmpIds             | string   | Comma-separated CC employee IDs (or "" to clear) |
  | ccPersonNames        | string   | Comma-separated CC names (or "" to clear)        |

  ## File attachments
  This route uses multer (`upload.array("files", 10)`) — send as `multipart/form-data` to add files.
  New files are appended; existing attachments are kept.
  ```
  curl -X PATCH http://<host>/api/requests/<id>/edit \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
    -F "purpose=Updated title" \
    -F "files=@/path/to/file.pdf"
  ```
  JSON body (no files) works fine for field-only edits.

  ## Errors
  - **403** — caller is not the requestor (or SuperUser)
  - **404** — request ID not found
  - **409** — requestor edit locked: someone has already acted / chatted on the request
}
